WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.292 --> 00:00:05.612
When flooding hit Butte's Covellite
Theatre, Montana Kush stepped up.

2
00:00:06.192 --> 00:00:07.872
A $4,800 gift.

3
00:00:08.472 --> 00:00:11.752
A relationship built through years of
concerts and community events.

4
00:00:12.492 --> 00:00:16.412
Across Montana, that commitment supports
food and winter clothing drives,

5
00:00:16.772 --> 00:00:19.412
blood drives, adult athletics, and local
arts.

6
00:00:20.092 --> 00:00:23.112
From Helena's Alive at Five to Bozeman's
Music on Main.

7
00:00:23.712 --> 00:00:27.472
Up to $350,000 in estimated community
support.

8
00:00:27.952 --> 00:00:32.072
Now, the Montana Kush Community Foundation
is building the next chapter.

9
00:00:32.572 --> 00:00:36.272
Local partnerships, veterans, education,
and community service.

10
00:00:36.952 --> 00:00:38.272
And your idea could be next.

11
00:00:38.932 --> 00:00:41.012
Applications are open for projects
statewide.

12
00:00:41.832 --> 00:00:47.252
$15,000 is available in awards of $500,
$1,000, or $1,500.

13
00:00:48.112 --> 00:00:50.712
Apply by December 15th, 2026.

14
00:00:51.392 --> 00:00:53.772
Awards announced January 2027.

15
00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:56.400
The Montana Kush Community Foundation.

16
00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:58.980
Supporting the communities that support
us.
